Does the fidelity budget transfer? configuration ariel

63 shared shift cases, six pipelines = 2 model families x 3 representations.
Spearman correlation of the per-case accuracy loss, every pair of pipelines.

pipeline A  pipeline B  relationship              rho
norm_xgb    pca_xgb     same model family       0.958
norm_rf     pca_rf      same model family       0.928
pca_xgb     raw_xgb     same model family       0.914
norm_xgb    raw_xgb     same model family       0.909
pca_rf      raw_rf      same model family       0.727
norm_rf     raw_rf      same model family       0.723
norm_xgb    norm_rf     same representation     0.983
pca_xgb     pca_rf      same representation     0.983
raw_xgb     raw_rf      same representation     0.826
norm_rf     pca_xgb     sharing neither         0.945
norm_xgb    pca_rf      sharing neither         0.930
norm_rf     raw_xgb     sharing neither         0.928
pca_rf      raw_xgb     sharing neither         0.925
norm_xgb    raw_rf      sharing neither         0.718
pca_xgb     raw_rf      sharing neither         0.695

physical proxy: Spearman(loss, surviving feature amplitude) = 0.289 (n = 63), so the ordering is not simply how much signal is left.

same representation    n=3  mean rho 0.931   range 0.826-0.983
same model family      n=6  mean rho 0.860   range 0.723-0.958
sharing neither        n=6  mean rho 0.857   range 0.695-0.945

same representation vs all other pairs:   Mann-Whitney U one-sided p = 0.0901   (n = 3 vs 12)
same representation vs same model family: Mann-Whitney U one-sided p = 0.1310
                                         permutation (20k) p = 0.2249
                                         mean difference = +0.071


Magnitude spread on the 29 cases costing at least 5 points to some pipeline:
  the same shift costs a median 4.8x more for one pipeline than another (max 48x).
  Between the two strongest pipelines alone it reaches 5.4x.

No ranking inversion under haze 3e7: frozen 96.05 -> 90.99%, PCA 91.84 -> 86.01%;
the in-domain ranking holds under the shift on this grid.

Sharing a model family agrees no better than sharing nothing (0.860 vs 0.857);
the representation is what carries the budget.
